### Requests for testing the API.
### In IntelliJ IDEA click the green arrow next to a request.
### Start the application first.

### 1. Create a user (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Smith",
  "email": "john@test.com",
  "age": 25
}

### 2. Get all users (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users

### 3. Get one user (expect 200, or 404 if the id does not exist)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/1

### 4. Update a user (expect 200, or 404 if the id does not exist)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Johnny",
  "lastName": "Smith",
  "email": "john@test.com",
  "age": 26
}

### 5. Delete a user (expect 204, or 404 if the id does not exist)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/users/1

### 6. Bad data (expect 400, because the email is not valid)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Bad",
  "lastName": "Email",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "age": 20
}
